                "entry_id": "00b9c7ee-88c7-369b-88b5-e0403fcd1eab",
                "word": "gepeins",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "78077800-0330-323d-862f-289486e04580",
                        "entry_id": "00b9c7ee-88c7-369b-88b5-e0403fcd1eab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "voortdurend heel diep (en vaak ook zorgelijk) nadenken"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b4aa96e-aa66-4b61-a9dc-ee949b0fde14",
                                "sense_id": "78077800-0330-323d-862f-289486e04580",
                                "text": "Met de Kerst in het vooruitzicht begint ook weer het jaarlijkse gepieker en gepeins over het kerstdiner."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a111823-6e83-4cb7-847a-3b1a38afafc1",
                                "sense_id": "78077800-0330-323d-862f-289486e04580",
                                "text": "Ze schrok op uit haar gepeins toen er op de deur werd geklopt. Nick leunde een beetje onhandig op zijn krukken, vooral omdat hij het met een hand ook nog een fles wijn vasthield. “Hi”, zei hij. “Heb jij glazen?” Zijn stem sloeg een beetje over. Kennelijk hoorde hij dat zelf ook want hij kreeg meteen een rood hoofd."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4987b708-dcdd-4c0a-b4da-0db4ab206db7",
                        "source_entry_id": "00b9c7ee-88c7-369b-88b5-e0403fcd1eab",
                        "source_sense_id": "78077800-0330-323d-862f-289486e04580",
                        "target_lang_word": "reverie",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "reverie",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2aa0dfcd-e3eb-33e3-acfb-2ae75a1ff911",
                                        "entry_id": "3cf48351-ab83-3c1f-9b8d-5a81aee24c6c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state of dreaming while awake; a loose or irregular train of thought; musing or meditation; daydream."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6592362-c5d3-42fa-a1c0-a5257fe389a5",
                                                "sense_id": "2aa0dfcd-e3eb-33e3-acfb-2ae75a1ff911",
                                                "text": "If you rouse from your reverie, you are restless and agitated; your eye wanders round in one perpetual search; and if, perchance, as has happened once or twice, he has only passed in the distance, your eye brightens, your cheek flushes crimson, and your whole frame quivers with uncontrollable emotion!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c157dce-165e-4715-869d-33a3368ee1b9",
                                                "sense_id": "2aa0dfcd-e3eb-33e3-acfb-2ae75a1ff911",
                                                "text": "we sat / But spoke not, rapt in nameless reverie, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "464d3e05-8f90-45a2-b831-abe93c3b50a9",
                                                "sense_id": "2aa0dfcd-e3eb-33e3-acfb-2ae75a1ff911",
                                                "text": "Within the branching shade of Reverie / Dreams even may spring till autumn; yet none be / ⁠Like woman's budding day-dream spirit-fann'd."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0c11366-4147-48b2-8e4a-b44b372484d8",
                                                "sense_id": "2aa0dfcd-e3eb-33e3-acfb-2ae75a1ff911",
                                                "text": "He fell into a reverie, a most dangerous state of mind for a chauffeur, since a fall into reverie on the part of a driver may mean a fall into a ravine on the part of the machine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b471d23-8329-4db2-972c-85ab0a2d68fe",
                                                "sense_id": "2aa0dfcd-e3eb-33e3-acfb-2ae75a1ff911",
                                                "text": "Even the blithely unselfconscious Homer is more than a little freaked out by West’s private reverie, and encourages his spawn to move slowly away without making eye contact with the crazy man."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15fcf566-1c2d-4cb5-b460-7dcc779442b3",
                                                "sense_id": "2aa0dfcd-e3eb-33e3-acfb-2ae75a1ff911",
                                                "text": "We were bound for eternity / Now I am lost inside this everlasting reverie / And I'm losing my mind"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24acb0e0-0367-31d6-af7e-d820c0b1f228",
                                        "entry_id": "3cf48351-ab83-3c1f-9b8d-5a81aee24c6c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An extravagant conceit of the imagination; a vision."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b03d2bd-3faf-4cad-ac2b-7e633a328d94",
                                                "sense_id": "24acb0e0-0367-31d6-af7e-d820c0b1f228",
                                                "text": "If the minds of men were laid open, we should see but little difference between that of the wise man and that of the fool; There are infinite reveries , numberless extravagancies , and a perpetual train of vanities , which pass through both ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "reverie",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36d3021c-775a-3dfa-bc0f-9f4f8b87227c",
                                        "entry_id": "6b010234-9031-3da9-b3b5-d55394ca2d42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To daydream."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c53d6ba-68f6-4e45-bf3e-7a3fc115a46e",
                                                "sense_id": "36d3021c-775a-3dfa-bc0f-9f4f8b87227c",
                                                "text": "By this time the mouth begins to feel uneasy—I pick another cheroot from Cotton’s last box, and walk up and down reverie-ing as before."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b50b2241-57c4-42a7-8dcf-8728d9b376ec",
                                                "sense_id": "36d3021c-775a-3dfa-bc0f-9f4f8b87227c",
                                                "text": "So now the dream of all my life is realized, and I have seen snow mountains! When I was quite a little child of eight years old I used to reverie about them, and when I heard the name of the snow-covered Sierra de la Summa Paz (perfect peace) the idea was completed; and I thenceforth always thought of eternal snow and perfect peace together, and longed to see the one and drink in the other."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47d925c3-0d09-4194-811a-99db579cfd92",
                                                "sense_id": "36d3021c-775a-3dfa-bc0f-9f4f8b87227c",
                                                "text": "During my twelfth and thirteenth years I often reveried in school, or less often at night, with penis quite erect—imagining perhaps myself in company with several of the girls that most attracted me on a Pacific Island, and I would feel and see myself again and again in sexual intercourse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d38ffa52-849c-45ca-b84c-f19ec33f14c0",
                                                "sense_id": "36d3021c-775a-3dfa-bc0f-9f4f8b87227c",
                                                "text": "In her old days she’ll either be Madame Representativewoman from the same said X-town, or a cheerful old philanderer, pardon me, I mean philanthropist, living in seclusion and reverying in the shades of the past."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8441d1a7-353b-4797-8f94-55f904252af0",
                                                "sense_id": "36d3021c-775a-3dfa-bc0f-9f4f8b87227c",
                                                "text": "He reveried on."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "reverie",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4ff80e1-ccfb-37e9-91c1-e7dfddad2f80",
                                        "entry_id": "93930fc3-6668-3cfe-8edd-bd6448ba22c6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A caper, a frolic; merriment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8dc10e30-ab6f-4ecf-8fe5-f0b20e44445f",
                        "source_entry_id": "00b9c7ee-88c7-369b-88b5-e0403fcd1eab",
                        "source_sense_id": "78077800-0330-323d-862f-289486e04580",
                        "target_lang_word": "deep-thinking",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ffef29c9-c2a6-4f67-b911-0ccede25c5bf",
                        "source_entry_id": "00b9c7ee-88c7-369b-88b5-e0403fcd1eab",
                        "source_sense_id": "78077800-0330-323d-862f-289486e04580",
                        "target_lang_word": "thought",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "thought",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c036027-2f12-3572-9ae5-502f028a5164",
                                        "entry_id": "1df5b7cc-733a-36e7-bb20-ac11f6f18c91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A representation created in the mind without the use of one's faculties of vision, sound, smell, touch, or taste; an instance of thinking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d6c0c65-f228-4b60-bfd5-44435ceb6c0d",
                                                "sense_id": "5c036027-2f12-3572-9ae5-502f028a5164",
                                                "text": "The greatest weapon against stress is our ability to choose one thought over another."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4181e4e-e0bf-4a64-b5fd-f3b26007610a",
                                                "sense_id": "5c036027-2f12-3572-9ae5-502f028a5164",
                                                "text": "I hate the thought of going back to work Monday morning."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b58b8cc-441b-49ec-b57f-fa8f07558344",
                                                "sense_id": "5c036027-2f12-3572-9ae5-502f028a5164",
                                                "text": "I corralled the judge, and we started off across the fields, in no very mild state of fear of that gentleman's wife, whose vigilance was seldom relaxed. And thus we came by a circuitous route to Mohair, the judge occupied by his own guilty thoughts, and I by others not less disturbing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e077b3f4-0039-4e0e-b1f8-06d3080da690",
                                                "sense_id": "5c036027-2f12-3572-9ae5-502f028a5164",
                                                "text": "He was thinking; but the glory of the song, the swell from the great organ, the clustered lights, […], the height and vastness of this noble fane, its antiquity and its strength—all these things seemed to have their part as causes of the thrilling emotion that accompanied his thoughts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5914baba-8727-3ddf-8325-ffcb015ca904",
                                        "entry_id": "1df5b7cc-733a-36e7-bb20-ac11f6f18c91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The operation by which mental activity arise or are manipulated; the process of thinking; the agency by which thinking is accomplished."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36a90c33-8d00-4e68-8555-5c4502dda253",
                                                "sense_id": "5914baba-8727-3ddf-8325-ffcb015ca904",
                                                "text": "Without freedom of thought there can be no such thing as wisdom, and no such thing as public liberty without freedom of speech."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a39daca-beda-4de1-8678-bf6daf370c1a",
                                                "sense_id": "5914baba-8727-3ddf-8325-ffcb015ca904",
                                                "text": "The only reason some people get lost in thought is because it’s unfamiliar territory."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12427aab-fcc5-4ffa-8ec2-210f817b6c5b",
                                                "sense_id": "5914baba-8727-3ddf-8325-ffcb015ca904",
                                                "text": "What has been especially striking in recent decades, however, is the rise of new outlooks challenging the very idea of a nucleated (if evasive) inner personal identity. … We don't think our thoughts, they think us; we are but the bearers of discourses, our selves are discursive constructs. Within such frames of analysis, any notion of the ascent of selfhood is but idle teleological myth, a humanist hagiography."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "679898ea-064f-3ea6-a0fe-82d21f81d8ac",
                                        "entry_id": "1df5b7cc-733a-36e7-bb20-ac11f6f18c91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A way of thinking (associated with a group, nation or region)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38209e57-a03b-48d4-8ff4-00b46f4ab334",
                                                "sense_id": "679898ea-064f-3ea6-a0fe-82d21f81d8ac",
                                                "text": "Traditional eastern thought differs markedly from that of the west."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b6e423ee-0bd0-3fff-bb39-359ef2648691",
                                        "entry_id": "1df5b7cc-733a-36e7-bb20-ac11f6f18c91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anxiety, distress."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dialectal",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "032447e8-cf05-484d-a7ae-d4c881f80152",
                                                "sense_id": "b6e423ee-0bd0-3fff-bb39-359ef2648691",
                                                "text": "Which of you by taking thought, can adde one cubite vnto his ſtature?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0ed93f4-eb90-36e8-a7a3-26f40a9b42a1",
                                        "entry_id": "1df5b7cc-733a-36e7-bb20-ac11f6f18c91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The careful consideration of multiple factors; deliberation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a324b90-72a1-42ae-b78a-b99560df0131",
                                                "sense_id": "c0ed93f4-eb90-36e8-a7a3-26f40a9b42a1",
                                                "text": "After much thought, I have decided to stay."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "649121bc-c40e-3953-ae96-46f7a29cb365",
                                        "entry_id": "1df5b7cc-733a-36e7-bb20-ac11f6f18c91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A very small amount, distance, etc.; a whit or jot."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9586198-f34b-41bd-b6f5-50ec79069338",
                                                "sense_id": "649121bc-c40e-3953-ae96-46f7a29cb365",
                                                "text": "'Bide the night at Heriotside,' says he. 'It's a thought out of your way, but it's a comfortable bit.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "thought",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c53d93e-bb59-3034-bda7-62adec12fb95",
